Week1 Card 8/25 Write Up: Dublin Under & Why FSU Blowout is My Favorite Play 🏈🚬

#KeepSwinging /#GoFrogs U48.5 -130 (HardRock) 1.8U
Back in June I was salivating at UNC and the points. I think Belichick coming to college with 18-22 yr olds & zero college coaching experience in the middle of NIL absurdity after almost 6 decades at the NFL level with grown professional men, and to get 4 wins in a Power4 conference that produced the national runner up was actually impressive. Especially considering they were closer to a bowl game than people realized. We picked their spots well last year & made us some money. But after coming up for air, seeing the summer unfold at Chapel Hill, and digging more into Billy Edwards Jr, I gotta see it to believe it before I jump on them. I know the hype on TCU and the team Dykes has this year, but I am also skeptical on Craig making an immediate jump from Ivy League to Power4 football. Even without Steve Belichick on sidelines, Bill will have his hands all over defense and I like that matchup vs Craig. I think Petrino will crawl then walk Billy Boy and the offense to start. Oh, and by the way did I mention the game is in Dublin? Unders are 3-0 there since 2023- the year the new clock stoppage rule was implemented. 

@FSUFootball -30.5 -115 (FanDuel) 1.8U
#NoleFamily 1H team total O23.5 -112 (fd) 1.3U
This is might be my favorite one for this weekend. If you saw my Futures Card, I think there’s tremendous value on the ceiling of this Seminole team with Ashton Daniels & OC Tim Harris Jr. Defense under Tony White expected to make year2 jump led by strong defensive line and secondary. And we haven’t even brought up Mike Norvell. Saturday night in Tallahassee will mean Doak Campbell will be rocking even if it’s just New Mexico State coming to town- it’s still the first football weekend of the year. Everything points to this team needing to come out flying under the lights. I like Ashton Daniels and the offense to get 3 TD and a FG in the first half or even a Defensive TD to help. While they will probably lock it down a bit second half with SMU upcoming, even with second offense Norvell needs to put a stamp early to boosters that they mean business this season and ramping up for SMU.

@uscfb team total O48.5 -132 (fd) 1.7U
Another one I am high on for a lot of similar reasons to Florida State. I flirted with Maiava as a darkhorse Heisman play this summer- he’s someone I’ve loved back when he was at UNLV. I think this returning offense is primed to be explosive this season and will want to show it early vs San Jose State. What made me feel even better about this was seeing @CoachBiggsCFB had this as his first post with VSiN. Couldn’t have broken it down any better. I really loved his last paragraph which much of that same reasoning was how I landed at this number in my process. Noon kick out West also another reason why stayed away from the spread, but love getting under the football number for team total. 

#GoBows +5.5 -130 (The Score) 1.7U;
@PackFootball +7 -139 (BetRivers) 1.5U
These 2 I put together because they were both games I told myself for the last month to most likely stay away since both opening matchups carry a lot of weight on their futures I’m already in on. But seeing the bet/money disparity and being able to get the numbers I could, it was hard for me to fully stay away. I know there’s the injury cloud around Ashlock for Hawaii, but nothing still scares me about Stanford that I need to run and hide from 5.5 points. Then getting a full touchdown, even in Charlottesville is something I couldn’t pass up. I’m more scared of the Virginia defense than anything the offense has to offer. I’ve been very down on Beau Pribula for a long time and I think CJ Bailey will prove to be the better playmaker when needed on Saturday
